  "foaf:name": "Digital Heritage Trails Project (DHTP)",
  "sdo:name": "Digital Heritage Trails Project (DHTP)",
  "sdo:description": "The Digital Heritage Trails Project records significant endangered archaeological sites in the Indus Delta region of Pakistan. Recognizing the vulnerability of these sites to climate change, the project seeks to preserve them digitally. By using non-intrusive techniques, the project has created high-resolution 3D models of the sites to support effective site management, monitoring, heritage conservation and the mitigation of climate-related impacts. The project enables a general public to “virtually visit” these historical places from anywhere in the world through a digital heritage trail. The trail is hosted on a website (www.lostcitiesofthedelta.org) and links historical information and community stories with the 3D site data to produce a unique interpretative experience for the visitor. Exploring a site virtually to explore and interrogate specific points of interest, pre-populated with rich interpretative content, provides for a unique tourism experience.",
  "sdo:location": "Pakistan",
  "sdo:identifier": "54.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/digital-heritage-trails-project-dhtp/",
  "sdo:license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
